1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,713
Part eight. Quotations.

2
00:00:04,250 --> 00:00:06,791
Open the lead and tap New quotation.

3
00:00:06,791 --> 00:00:10,249
The lead becomes a customer if it is not one yet,

4
00:00:10,249 --> 00:00:13,920
and the quotation opens with the customer filled in.

5
00:00:14,810 --> 00:00:17,665
Type the system size in kilowatts.

6
00:00:17,665 --> 00:00:23,038
Then add lines: choose a product and its description, HSN, unit,

7
00:00:23,038 --> 00:00:26,984
price and GST rate come from your product list.

8
00:00:26,984 --> 00:00:30,678
Panels and inverters carry five percent GST.

9
00:00:31,570 --> 00:00:38,260
Add the structure, and installation, which is a service at eighteen percent.

10
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:45,478
The totals below show the taxable value, CGST and SGST, or IGST for another state,

11
00:00:45,478 --> 00:00:47,062
and the round-off.

12
00:00:47,970 --> 00:00:55,842
Give a discount in rupees if you agreed one; GST is worked out after the discount.

13
00:00:55,842 --> 00:00:56,322
Save.

14
00:00:56,322 --> 00:01:01,218
The quotation gets its number, like QT slash 26-27.

15
00:01:02,130 --> 00:01:04,356
Print or save it as PDF.

16
00:01:04,356 --> 00:01:11,125
It shows your logo and GSTIN, the lines with HSN, taxes, amount in words,

17
00:01:11,125 --> 00:01:15,947
your bank details, and the estimated units per year,

18
00:01:15,947 --> 00:01:19,378
savings and payback for the customer.

19
00:01:20,290 --> 00:01:25,054
Share on WhatsApp opens the quotation message for the customer.

20
00:01:25,054 --> 00:01:29,137
Save the PDF, open WhatsApp and attach it in the chat.

21
00:01:30,050 --> 00:01:33,381
When the customer agrees, tap Confirm order.

22
00:01:33,381 --> 00:01:36,787
The quotation becomes Accepted, the lead Won,

23
00:01:36,787 --> 00:01:40,270
and a project is started for the installation.

24
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:45,807
Next video: GST invoices, payments and receipts.

